{
 "schema": 2,
 "name": "foilsnopa_bc",
 "note": "Stopping target with no inner or outer proton absorber (the inner one is not built, the outer one is DS vacuum, their supports are off), the foilsflash_ax extra foils (37 fixed + 6 up + 6 down) and a target shift toward the tracker, on SimJob MDC2025bc. It steers on S/sqrt(B) and the busiest tracker-region hit rate. The busiest-channel tracker rate is edep_occupancy_combine's busiest region (12 planes x 8 straw numbers x the six panels, the mean per straw; unbiased at a design point's statistics, unlike a single row) in the digitizers' event window, from three pileup components each normalized per generated event (gen_events_per_pot) at 1.58e7 POT per microbunch; the beam-flash neutrons and gammas are left out. Design: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-30-foilsnopa-study-design.md, revision 2026-11-05 (local).",
 "knobs": [
  {
   "name": "extra_rOut_up",
   "type": "real",
   "min": 50.0,
   "max": 250.0,
   "unit": "",
   "fmt": "{:.4f}"
  },
  {
   "name": "extra_rOut_dn",
   "type": "real",
   "min": 50.0,
   "max": 250.0,
   "unit": "",
   "fmt": "{:.4f}"
  },
  {
   "name": "extra_halfThickness_up",
   "type": "real",
   "min": 0.002,
   "max": 1.0,
   "unit": "",
   "fmt": "{:.6f}"
  },
  {
   "name": "extra_halfThickness_dn",
   "type": "real",
   "min": 0.002,
   "max": 1.0,
   "unit": "",
   "fmt": "{:.6f}"
  },
  {
   "name": "extra_f_up",
   "type": "real",
   "min": 0.0,
   "max": 0.95,
   "unit": "",
   "fmt": "{:.4f}"
  },
  {
   "name": "extra_f_dn",
   "type": "real",
   "min": 0.0,
   "max": 0.95,
   "unit": "",
   "fmt": "{:.4f}"
  },
  {
   "name": "target_dz",
   "type": "real",
   "min": 0.0,
   "max": 1900.0,
   "unit": "",
   "fmt": "{:.2f}"
  }
 ],
 "derive": {
  "consts": {
   "n_up": 6,
   "n_dn": 6,
   "base_n": 37,
   "base_rOut": 75.0,
   "base_hT": 0.0528,
   "base_hole": 21.5,
   "z0_nominal": 5871.0
  },
  "exprs": {
   "rIn_up": "extra_f_up * extra_rOut_up",
   "rIn_dn": "extra_f_dn * extra_rOut_dn",
   "z0_st": "z0_nominal + target_dz"
  },
  "profiles": {}
 },
 "geom": {
  "writer": "offline_simpleconfig",
  "base": "Offline/Mu2eG4/geom/geom_run1_a.txt",
  "lines": [
   {
    "comment": "=== foilsnopa (7D: foilsflash extras + target_dz, no IPA, no OPA) ==="
   },
   {
    "comment": "{base_n} base foils (DOE-2017, rOut={base_rOut}, hT={base_hT}, holeRadius={base_hole})"
   },
   {
    "comment": "+ {n_up} up at (rOut={extra_rOut_up:.2f}, hT={extra_halfThickness_up:.4f}, rIn={rIn_up:.2f})"
   },
   {
    "comment": "+ {n_dn} dn at (rOut={extra_rOut_dn:.2f}, hT={extra_halfThickness_dn:.4f}, rIn={rIn_dn:.2f})"
   },
   {
    "comment": "holeRadii vector decouples extras-rIn from base-rIn (patched lib)."
   },
   {
    "comment": "EMC_Source relocated 5300 -> 5000. It is a 20um disc of ds.vacuumMaterial (vd.halfLength=0.01) -- ZERO mass, no scattering, no absorption -- and NO foils-family stage reads virtual detectors (only pot_only instantiates ReadVirtualDetector). At 5300 it was the UPSTREAM wall of the zero-overlap corridor, capping the stack at 6271-5300=971mm. zEMCSourceInMu2e is a plain c.getDouble default at VirtualDetectorMaker.cc:189, so this is one config line, no source patch. EMC_Source2 stays at 4800, so ordering is preserved."
   },
   {
    "key": "zEMCSourceInMu2e",
    "type": "double",
    "value": 5000.0
   },
   {
    "comment": "No inner and no outer proton absorber. Offline v13_44_00 builds hasProtonAbsorber=false (PR #2089), but without the outer absorber the virtual detectors ST_In, ST_Out and STMUpstream take the DS2 bore minus 5 mm (constructVirtualDetectors.cc) and overlap Coupler_DS2_1 and others, so the absorbers stay but are inert: protonabsorber.ipa.build=false drops the IPA and its wires and end rings; the OPA is filled with DS vacuum (outerPAMaterialName covers both sections) and kept only for those detectors' radius; oPASupportNSupportRing=0 skips the whole OPA support block: the rings, the cross supports and the target support slats."
   },
   {
    "key": "protonabsorber.ipa.build",
    "type": "bool",
    "value": false
   },
   {
    "key": "protonabsorber.outerPAMaterialName",
    "type": "string",
    "value": "DSVacuum"
   },
   {
    "key": "protonabsorber.oPASupportNSupportRing",
    "type": "int",
    "value": 0
   },
   {
    "comment": "The unbuilt IPA is still computed: zStartInMu2e keeps it at its hardware position 6901.02-7901.02 (upstream in v13_43_00) instead of following the target end."
   },
   {
    "key": "protonabsorber.zStartInMu2e",
    "type": "double",
    "value": 6901.02
   },
   {
    "comment": "Target shift toward the tracker: z0 = 5871 + target_dz. At 1900 mm the 49-foil mother (half-length 538.33) ends at 8309.3, 29.7 mm inside DS2Vacuum (to 8339)."
   },
   {
    "key": "stoppingTarget.z0InMu2e",
    "type": "double",
    "expr": "z0_st",
    "fmt": "{:.4f}"
   },
   {
    "key": "hasTSdA",
    "type": "bool",
    "value": false
   },
   {
    "key": "tsda.helical.build",
    "type": "bool",
    "value": false
   },
   {
    "key": "stoppingTarget.radii",
    "type": "vector<double>",
    "fmt": "{:.4f}",
    "segments": [
     {
      "count": "n_up",
      "expr": "extra_rOut_up"
     },
     {
      "count": "base_n",
      "expr": "base_rOut"
     },
     {
      "count": "n_dn",
      "expr": "extra_rOut_dn"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "key": "stoppingTarget.halfThicknesses",
    "type": "vector<double>",
    "fmt": "{:.6f}",
    "segments": [
     {
      "count": "n_up",
      "expr": "extra_halfThickness_up"
     },
     {
      "count": "base_n",
      "expr": "base_hT"
     },
     {
      "count": "n_dn",
      "expr": "extra_halfThickness_dn"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "comment": "POISON PILL: an unpatched StoppingTargetMaker ignores holeRadii and reads"
   },
   {
    "comment": "this scalar. 1e6 forces a loud G4Tubs crash instead of a silently uniform"
   },
   {
    "comment": "stack -- emitting a 'sensible' scalar is how 62 foilsg rows were lost."
   },
   {
    "key": "stoppingTarget.holeRadius",
    "type": "double",
    "raw": "1.0e6"
   },
   {
    "key": "stoppingTarget.holeRadii",
    "type": "vector<double>",
    "fmt": "{:.4f}",
    "segments": [
     {
      "count": "n_up",
      "expr": "rIn_up"
     },
     {
      "count": "base_n",
      "expr": "base_hole"
     },
     {
      "count": "n_dn",
      "expr": "rIn_dn"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "comment": "Degrader parked at 120 deg (mmackenz hardware detent)"
   },
   {
    "key": "degrader.build",
    "type": "bool",
    "value": false
   },
   {
    "key": "degrader.rotation",
    "type": "double",
    "value": 120.0
   },
   {
    "key": "ts.coll5.material1Name",
    "type": "string",
    "value": "COL5Poly"
   },
   {
    "comment": "TT_MidInner -> DS2Vacuum workaround REMOVED 2026-07-28 (Run1Bap migration). Under v13_12_10 constructVirtualDetectors:502 parented the tracker VDs on `isDumbbell` (always false here), nailing them into DS2Vacuum while Mu2eWorld:346 put the tracker itself in DS3Vacuum -- VDs protruded 1.8-3.5 m outside their mother, GeomMgt0002 fatal. Forcing tracker.inDS2Vacuum=true + ds2.halfLength=3825 made the two agree. v13_32_10 keys VD parenting on !tracker.inDS2Vacuum, so stock is self-consistent and the workaround is not just redundant but harmful: it re-parented EMC_0_Front into DS2Vacuum as a sibling of StoppingTargetMother, which WAS the last remaining overlap. Measured 2x2 on foilspf corner_hi: Run1Bak+override 1 overlap, Run1Bap+override 1, Run1Bak-override 6 + rc=134 core dump, Run1Bap-override 0."
   },
   {
    "key": "ds.hasServicePipes",
    "type": "bool",
    "value": false
   },
   {
    "comment": "Overlap-suppression (foil-support off + rail shrink)"
   },
   {
    "key": "stoppingTarget.foilTarget_supportStructure",
    "type": "bool",
    "value": false
   },
   {
    "key": "ds.lengthRail2",
    "type": "double",
    "value": 0.1
   },
   {
    "key": "ds.lengthRail3",
    "type": "double",
    "value": 0.1
   }
  ]
 },
